<div id="printpocket_settings">
<h3>PrintPocket</h3>

<p>
  On your phone, open
  <a href="{{ url_for('plugin.printpocket.app_index') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-bind="text: appUrl"></span></a>
  and add it to your Home Screen. Use this computer's address for the Pi, or its VPN name (for example
  <code>http://octopi.netbird.cloud/plugin/printpocket/</code>).
</p>

<h4>Pair a phone</h4>
<p class="muted">Gives a phone its own key, so it never needs your OctoPrint password. Type the code into PrintPocket on the phone.</p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 18px">
  <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: newCode, disable: pairing">Show a pairing code</button>
  <span data-bind="visible: code" style="margin-left: 14px">
    <strong data-bind="text: codePretty" style="font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 4px; font-family: monospace; vertical-align: middle"></strong>
    <span class="muted" style="margin-left: 8px">valid for 10 minutes, works once</span>
  </span>
</div>

<form class="form-horizontal" onsubmit="return false;">
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Printer name</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-large" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.printer_name" placeholder="Defaults to the OctoPrint instance name">
      <span class="help-block">Shown in notifications and under the home screen icon.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">App address</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.app_url" placeholder="http://octopi.netbird.cloud/plugin/printpocket/">
      <span class="help-block">Where tapping a notification takes you. Optional.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Progress every</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" min="0" max="50" step="5" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.progress_step">
        <span class="add-on">%</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Step for progress notifications. 0 turns them off.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Notifications with ntfy</h4>
  <p class="muted">
    Works over NetBird or any VPN, no HTTPS needed. Install the free <strong>ntfy</strong> app on your phone,
    create a topic below, save, then in the app tap + and paste the same topic URL.
    The long random name is what keeps it private, so don't share it.
  </p>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Topic URL</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.ntfy_url" placeholder="https://ntfy.sh/printpocket-...">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: newTopic">New topic</button>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Use your own ntfy server by replacing <code>https://ntfy.sh</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Access token</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="password" class="input-large" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.ntfy_token" placeholder="Only for protected topics">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Send me</label>
    <div class="controls" data-bind="foreach: events">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checkedValue: key, checked: $parent.settings.plugins.printpocket.ntfy_events"> <span data-bind="text: label"></span>
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.printpocket.ntfy_snapshot"> Attach a webcam picture (finished, failed, paused, errors)
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <button class="btn" data-bind="click: testNtfy, disable: testing">Send a test</button>
      <span class="muted" style="margin-left: 8px">Save first if you changed the topic.</span>
      <span data-bind="text: testResult" style="margin-left: 8px"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Web Push</h4>
  <p class="muted">
    Notifications straight to the PrintPocket icon, without the ntfy app. Phones only allow this on an
    <code>https://</code> address, so it needs HTTPS on the Pi (for example <code>tailscale serve</code>).
    Each phone turns it on in its Alerts tab.
  </p>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Push contact</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.printpocket.vapid_subject">
      <span class="help-block">A <code>mailto:</code> address included in push requests. Any address of yours works.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
</div>
